# Recipes for NAT instances. Empty on purpose.
#
# Anything a NAT needs at boot belongs in user-data, where a change
# replaces the box — which is correct for something that defines what the
# box IS. A recipe is for changing a box that is already RUNNING and
# routing, where replacing it would cost the region its egress.
#
# The runner is wired and handles an empty set, so adding a numbered
# script here is the whole procedure. The directory has to exist for
# fileset() to read it, which is why this file is here.
